# Search-Detect-Land — ArduCopter 4.6.3 parameter changes
# Derived from dataflash logs 79 / 80 / 81 (2026-08-02), which ended in a crash.
# Load in Mission Planner: Config > Full Parameter Tree > Load from file > Write Params
#
# Two root causes were found:
#   1. A 10 Hz limit cycle in the rate controller (measured loop gain 0.99).
#      This is the "shaking". Not props, not vibration - pre-filter gyro noise
#      above 15 Hz is under 5 deg/s RMS while the oscillation is 40 deg/s.
#   2. MOT_THST_HOVER was 0.3297 while real hover throttle is 0.108. The mixer
#      floors average throttle at MOT_THST_HOVER * ATC_THR_MIX_MAX = 0.165,
#      which is ABOVE hover -> uncommanded 2.5 m/s climb in AltHold with the
#      throttle stick on the bottom stop. That is what crashed it.
#
# Battery failsafe ACTIONS are left commented out - decide those yourself.

# --- 1. CRASH FIX: hover throttle was 3x too high ---
MOT_THST_HOVER,0.11                 # was 0.3297; measured hover ThO = 0.108

# --- 2. 6S battery (README previously said 4S; logs show 24.12 V at arm) ---
MOT_BAT_VOLT_MAX,25.2               # was 0 (thrust/voltage compensation off)
MOT_BAT_VOLT_MIN,19.8               # was 0
BATT_LOW_VOLT,21.0                  # was 10.5 (a 3S value - could never fire)
BATT_CRT_VOLT,19.8                  # was 0
# BATT_FS_LOW_ACT,1                 # 0 = warn only, 1 = Land. RTL needs GPS.
# BATT_FS_CRT_ACT,1

# --- 3. Radio failsafe margin ---
# TX sends 982 us at throttle-bottom; trip point was 975. 7 us is not margin.
# Also redo the RC calibration: RC1_MIN reads 1002 but the TX sends 982.
FS_THR_VALUE,950                    # was 975

# --- 4. Kill the 10 Hz oscillation ---
# Loop gain as-flown 0.99 (sustained). These put it at 0.52 => 5.7 dB margin.
# D was the dominant term: 0.134 of the 0.198 output at 10 Hz, vs 0.094 for P.
# Leave ATC_RAT_*_FLTD and *_FLTT at 20 - moving the gyro filter to 40 restores
# the intended FLTD = gyro_filter/2 relationship without editing them.
INS_GYRO_FILTER,40                  # was 20 (a 12"+ prop default; costs 26.6
                                    # deg of phase lag at 10 Hz, 14.0 at 40 Hz)
ATC_RAT_RLL_P,0.08                  # was 0.135
ATC_RAT_RLL_I,0.08                  # was 0.135 (kept equal to P by convention)
ATC_RAT_RLL_D,0.0015                # was 0.0036
ATC_RAT_PIT_P,0.08                  # was 0.135
ATC_RAT_PIT_I,0.08                  # was 0.135
ATC_RAT_PIT_D,0.0015                # was 0.0036
# Yaw: precautionary only. Yaw was NOT driving the oscillation (its output at
# 10 Hz measured 5 units vs 6865 in the gyro). First thing to put back if yaw
# feels sluggish after the retune.
ATC_RAT_YAW_P,0.09                  # was 0.18
ATC_RAT_YAW_I,0.009                 # was 0.018

# --- 5. No GPS is fitted; stop telling the EKF to expect one ---
# EKF altitude was drifting up to 3.5 m away from baro mid-flight.
# Leave EK3_SRC1_POSZ = 1 (Baro) and EK3_SRC1_YAW = 1 (Compass) alone.
# When the AprilTag pose feed is live, POSXY/VELXY become 6 (ExternalNav).
EK3_SRC1_POSXY,0                    # was 3 (GPS)
EK3_SRC1_VELXY,0                    # was 3 (GPS)
EK3_SRC1_VELZ,0                     # was 3 (GPS)

# --- Not parameters, but same priority ---
# * Inspect the airframe first. It fell 8 m. Arms, motor bells, prop shafts,
#   FC mounting. A tune measured on a bent frame is worthless.
# * Put Stabilize on the mode switch's RESTING position, and physically
#   separate the arm switch from it (the crash ended in an aux-switch disarm
#   at 7.97 m that was meant to be AltHold -> Stabilize).
#
# --- Test sequence ---
# 1. Flight 1: Stabilize only, ~1 m, hover 30-60 s.
# 2. Pull the log, check three things:
#      - RATE.R  : is the 10 Hz peak gone or much smaller?
#      - RCOU    : are motors still pinned at 1090 (they were 82% of the time)?
#      - CTUN.ThO at steady hover -> that is your true MOT_THST_HOVER.
# 3. Still oscillating? Halve D again. One change at a time.
# 4. Flight 2: AltHold, still low. Confirm it holds AND descends when asked.
# 5. Then AUTOTUNE, one axis at a time via AUTOTUNE_AXES.
#
# Keep LOG_BITMASK as-is - the fast attitude logging is what made this
# measurable in the first place.
